      "text": [
        " «إِذَا زَالَتِ اَلشَّمْسُ فَقَدْ دَخَلَ وَقْتُ اَلصَّلاَتَيْنِ فَإِذَا فَرَغْتَ مِنْ سُبْحَتِكَ فَصَلِّ اَلظُّهْرَ مَتَى مَا بَدَا لَكَ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.646 - Malik Al-Juhani asked Imam Jafar ibn Muhammad Al-Sadiq (as) about the time for the Dhuhr (noon) prayer.\nImam (as) replied: \"When the sun declines (from its zenith), the time for both (Dhuhr and Asr) prayers begins. So, when you finish your Nawafil (supererogatory prayer), you may perform the Dhuhr prayer whenever you wish.\""
        ]
      }
